{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-32973-r4517373","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Chicken Biryani","sourcePageId":32973,"sourceRevision":"4517373","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T02:10:28Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Chicken%20Biryani&oldid=4517373","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:35:22.708Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Baked recipes","Category:Indian recipes","Category:Main course recipes","Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for biryani","Category:Recipes using cardamom","Category:Recipes using chicken","Category:Recipes using chile","Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick","Category:Recipes using cumin","Category:Recipes using fresh ginger","Category:Recipes using garlic","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes using yogurt","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"c3c45ef09b482e932b38d2915059d6eddc3054f774507c63af7cb6d9c8364a9f","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary\n| Category = Rice recipes\n| Servings = 2\n| Difficulty = 3\n| Image = [[File:Chicken Dum Biriyani.JPG|Chicken_Dum_Biriyani|300px]]\n}}\n{{recipe}}\n==Ingredients==\n* 2 [[Cookbook:cup|cup]]s [[cookbook:rice|rice]] (preferably Basmati)               \t\n* 500 [[Cookbook:gram|g]] (1 [[Cookbook:Pound|lb]]) [[cookbook:chicken|chicken]]\n* 6 [[Cookbook:tablespoon|tablespoon]]s [[cookbook:oil|oil]]\n* 300 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]] (10 [[Cookbook:Ounce|oz]]) [[cookbook:yogurt|yoghurt]]\n* 3 cloves of [[cookbook:garlic|garlic]], crushed and [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 1.5 [[Cookbook:Centimetre (cm)|cm]] [[cookbook:ginger|ginger]], peeled and [[Cookbook:Slicing|sliced]]\n\n* 5 large [[cookbook:onion|onion]]s, chopped\n* ½ cup [[cookbook:tomato|tomato]]es, [[Cookbook:Puréeing|puréed]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Chiles|chiles]], chopped\n* 1 [[Cookbook:teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[cookbook:turmeric|turmeric]] powder\n* 5–6 strands [[cookbook:saffron|saffron]]\n* 8 [[cookbook:clove|clove]]s\n* 10 cm (4 [[Cookbook:Inch|inches]]) [[cookbook:cinnamon|cinnamon]] stick\n* 5 [[cookbook:pepper|black pepper]] corns\n* 8 [[cookbook:cardamom|cardamom]] pods\n* 1 teaspoon [[cookbook:cumin|cumin]]\n* [[cookbook:Salt|Salt]] to taste\n\n==Procedure==\n[[Image:Biryani preparation.jpg|right|thumb|250px|Chicken biryani being prepared for 2000 people in Bidar, India.]]\n# Cook soaked and washed rice.\n# [[cookbook:Marinating|Marinate]] the chicken in [[cookbook:Lemon Juice|lemon juice]], yoghurt, ginger, garlic, salt, turmeric powder, cumin powder, cloves, chillis, chopped tomatoes, and tomato purée.\n# Heat oil in a pan, add onions, and cook until onions turn golden brown. Add these to the chicken.\n# Grease a heavy-bottomed deep and wide mouthed pan. Add a layer of rice. Put in the chicken mixture, top with the rest of the rice, and put the saffron on top.\n# Bake in the oven for 1–1½ hours at 150°C (300°F); cut into a piece of chicken to see if it is cooked.\n# Serve the biryani with yoghurt on the side.\n\n== External links ==\n* [http://showmethecurry.com/2008/02/04/chicken-biryani/ Chicken Biryani Video Demonstration]\n* [http://www.currydishes.com/Indian-Recipes/chicken-biryani.html Recipe for making Chicken Biryani]\n* [http://briyani.net Briyani.Net] An website exclusively dedicated for Biryani and allied dishes\n\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes using yogurt]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cumin]]\n[[Category:Indian recipes]]\n[[Category:Baked recipes]]\n[[Category:Main course recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes with metric units]]\n[[Category:Recipes for biryani]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cardamom]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cinnamon stick]]\n[[Category:Recipes using garlic]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fresh ginger]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Chicken Biryani","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"2","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"2 cups rice (preferably Basmati)","sourceText":"2 cups rice (preferably Basmati)","amountText":"2 cups rice (preferably Basmati)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"500 g (1 lb) chicken","sourceText":"500 g (1 lb) chicken","amountText":"500 g (1 lb) chicken","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"6 tablespoons oil","sourceText":"6 tablespoons oil","amountText":"6 tablespoons oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"300 ml (10 oz) yoghurt","sourceText":"300 ml (10 oz) yoghurt","amountText":"300 ml (10 oz) yoghurt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"3 cloves of garlic, crushed and chopped","sourceText":"3 cloves of garlic, crushed and chopped","amountText":"3 cloves of garlic, crushed and chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"1.5 cm ginger, peeled and sliced","sourceText":"1.5 cm ginger, peeled and sliced","amountText":"1.5 cm ginger, peeled and sliced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"5 large onions, chopped","sourceText":"5